body:
**2026-11-02 — Schema BCAP O1/O2 returns submitted (Revise)**

I submit these Schema design-review dispositions against manifest `ff475d712f6ef6aa5033113cc39afb887ae4cbad24705098c5c9cb2097641688`. Both decisions are **Revise**, not acceptance. Matching JSON response files are in the unsealed `docs/foundation-bcap-owner-review/returns/` area. Both pass `tools/returns.py`; this validates form completeness and draft binding only, not signer identity, substantive acceptance, runtime qualification, C45 or API freeze. Responses are Copilot-authored on explicit user direction; the designated signer is recorded as provided but has not been independently authenticated.

### BCAP-O1-Schema

```json
{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "returnId": "BCAP-O1-Schema",
  "packet": "BCAP-O1",
  "owner": "Schema",
  "proposalManifestSha256": "ff475d712f6ef6aa5033113cc39afb887ae4cbad24705098c5c9cb2097641688",
  "responseStatus": "Submitted",
  "decision": "Revise",
  "sourceRevision": "20090180755d0427d824b091cf838e9a03ca9adc",
  "signer": "Copilot - Schema design reviewer, submitted on explicit user direction; designated signer fytala-charles@fytala.com (not independently authenticated)",
  "date": "2026-11-02",
  "profile": "Schema source/design disposition only, bound to the exact BCAP manifest. Public Bosak.Schema checkout reviewed at 20090180755d0427d824b091cf838e9a03ca9adc; the separate native assessor candidate is pinned by the owner audit at c3624998eca8c83018e121fa84af611f834a0501 and is not present in this checkout for method-level verification. The bounded native profile is exact-decimal leaves and an element-only root with no typed value. No public SDK implementation, native adapter integration, R4 runtime qualification, C45 acceptance, API freeze or product adoption is claimed.",
  "answers": [
    {
      "id": "O1-Q1",
      "answer": "The contract is that the trusted input owner establishes exact live source/snapshot membership before any getter is called on a purported node, without copying/materializing the graph; this is ordinary source membership, not schema authority. The owner audit identifies XsdDocumentAssessor.Assess and AssessedDocument.CreateDocumentCopy, but neither is shown to be the concrete membership predicate, and this checkout does not contain the pinned native assessor source. I therefore cannot supply a verified native method implementing ISchemaAssessmentInput.OwnsNode or claim the before-getter case is qualified. The exact method mapping and negative foreign-node evidence remain required for the native profile. XmlDb's persistent source membership is a separate owner disposition and is not claimed here."
    },
    {
      "id": "O1-Q2",
      "answer": "Required invariant: facts are bound to the exact node, input snapshot and original origin/assessment. The revised advisor association check OwnsNode(node, facts, input, origin), in addition to OwnsNodeFacts and input membership, must authenticate that tuple; copied facts or component handles with matching QNames/digests do not. Preserve-copy may retain original PSVI only if the provider can prove the copied node's association with the original evidence and bind it to the new snapshot; otherwise strip facts and reassess. Any edit that can stale evidence must invalidate/strip it or require reassessment. Independently compiled components remain distinct authority. The owner audit says AssessedDocument.Copy preserves original assessment/component references while creating a new snapshot identity and that supported annotations can be preserved or stripped, but no method-level copy mapping or stale-edit qualification is available here; implementation proof remains open."
    },
    {
      "id": "O1-Q3",
      "answer": "ReadTypedValue must be called through the exact admitted SchemaQuerySnapshot. Before reading any typed-value container member or enumerating its atomics, the bound advisor must verify OwnsTypedValue(value, input, originalAssessment), with the exact admitted input and optional original assessment; each atomic's current type/provenance must then be checked against the same authority and snapshot. Ordinary unassessed XmlDb XML has no assessor, advisor or original assessment, and must not receive fabricated Schema facts; schema-issued typed-value checks are not applicable to that profile. Fresh construction supplies current constructed type evidence only and does not mint original PSVI. The proposed public operation bodies throw, and no production implementation of this ordering is claimed."
    },
    {
      "id": "O1-Q4",
      "answer": "Feasibility plan against native candidate c3624998eca8c83018e121fa84af611f834a0501: (1) same admitted input and native decimal leaf succeeds; (2) a node from another snapshot, instrumented so any getter fails the test, is rejected by OwnsNode before that getter; (3) a preserved copy succeeds only with an authenticated old-to-new node/facts/origin mapping, while the strip-copy has no original facts and requires reassessment; (4) edit after preservation invalidates/rejects the old facts; (5) an independently compiled component handle is rejected despite matching name/digest; and (6) revocation prevents further node or typed-value reads. The available audit supports only a bounded decimal profile and does not supply these executed cases or the exact membership method. No additional required public signature is identified from the packet; method mapping and source-specific cases remain the reasons for Revise, not a claim that runtime qualification has occurred."
    }
  ],
  "unresolvedRequiredSignatureGaps": [],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "kind": "SourceMapping",
      "reference": "Bosak.Schema public source revision 20090180755d0427d824b091cf838e9a03ca9adc; the public checkout contains no native XsdDocumentAssessor/AssessedDocument source mapping for ISchemaAssessmentInput.OwnsNode."
    },
    {
      "kind": "DesignDisposition",
      "reference": "BCAP manifest ff475d712f6ef6aa5033113cc39afb887ae4cbad24705098c5c9cb2097641688; REVIEW.md R01-R08; O1 questions in PACKETS.json; proposal inputs/proposal/Provider.cs.txt and QueryFacade.cs.txt. Proposed declarations are not a production implementation."
    },
    {
      "kind": "DesignDisposition",
      "reference": "Bosak/docs/release-planning/OWNER-CAPABILITIES.md: bounded native decimal profile, separate assessment/snapshot identities, preserve/strip behavior and missing production adapter binding; native candidate c3624998eca8c83018e121fa84af611f834a0501."
    },
    {
      "kind": "DesignDisposition",
      "reference": "Bosak.Schema.Public/docs/XSD11_GAP_MATRIX.md and docs/AGENT_HANDOVER.md: full XSD 1.1 and core session/PSVI integration remain incomplete; no public Schema BCAP runtime qualification is inferred."
    }
  ],
  "runtimeQualification": false,
  "c45Accepted": false,
  "apiFrozen": false,
  "priorReturnId": "O1-Schema",
  "reviewMode": "MissingFullReturn",
  "deltaApplicability": "R01: capture entry/result APIs do not establish native source membership; the source owner must still check exact membership before foreign getters and must not eagerly copy the graph. The public proposal bodies throw, and no native capture route is qualified. R02: serialized capture outputs are not XDM nodes, schema authority or retained PSVI; no new Schema membership claim follows. R03: preserve Schema execution/validation failure identity locally and keep it distinct from capture/cleanup failure; do not infer successful validation from a capture envelope. R04: no new Schema-specific input limits or capture policy were qualified here; finite operation/numeric policies still require explicit adoption at their relevant boundary. R05: capture must remain within the same raw operation and retain actual provider resources through work/cleanup; no Schema lease/resource transfer is implied. R06: original exception graphs are local diagnostic references only and do not authorize node getters or traversal after revocation. R07: Core private measurements are not Schema workload budgets or native performance qualification. R08: this is Revise for this exact design review; no C45, API-freeze, public SDK, native integration or release acceptance is implied.",
  "originalExceptionGraphDisposition": "Schema/provider exceptions and capture diagnostics may be retained only as local diagnostic references with original identity and aggregate boundaries preserved. They are not detached, immutable, sanitized or safe for IPC. Do not recursively inspect Exception.Data, InnerException, arbitrary provider payloads or node-bearing objects, especially after revocation; do not publish raw exception graphs. If export is needed, require an owner-controlled bounded allowlist/projection and redaction policy. Capture or exception retention confers no Schema authority and does not establish release success.",
  "acceptedPerformanceBudgets": null,
  "priorResponseSha256": null
}
```

### BCAP-O2-Schema

```json
{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "returnId": "BCAP-O2-Schema",
  "packet": "BCAP-O2",
  "owner": "Schema",
  "proposalManifestSha256": "ff475d712f6ef6aa5033113cc39afb887ae4cbad24705098c5c9cb2097641688",
  "responseStatus": "Submitted",
  "decision": "Revise",
  "sourceRevision": "20090180755d0427d824b091cf838e9a03ca9adc",
  "signer": "Copilot - Schema design reviewer, submitted on explicit user direction; designated signer fytala-charles@fytala.com (not independently authenticated)",
  "date": "2026-11-02",
  "profile": "Schema source/design disposition only, bound to the exact BCAP manifest. Public Bosak.Schema checkout reviewed at 20090180755d0427d824b091cf838e9a03ca9adc; native assessor candidate c3624998eca8c83018e121fa84af611f834a0501 is a separate audited lane. The bounded backend evidence is decimal-only and does not establish general list/union, complete XSD 1.1 authority or compatible-universe support. No public SDK implementation, native integration, R4 qualification, accepted performance budgets, C45 acceptance, API freeze or product adoption is claimed.",
  "answers": [
    {
      "id": "O2-Q1",
      "answer": "Retain the six proposed XdmValue intents: FromInteger(BigInteger), its schema-name overload, BigIntegerValue, FromDecimal(XdmExactDecimal), its schema-name overload, and ExactDecimalValue. XdmExactDecimal is a normalized exact finite coefficient/nonnegative-scale representation, with zero normalized to scale zero. Preserve existing wrong-kind checks; legacy narrowing must refuse overflow or inexact conversion, never round. BigIntegerValue accepts integer kind and only recognized decimal-backed integer representations, not an ordinary decimal; ExactDecimalValue accepts decimal kind and the specified integer-tagged decimal representation while refusing Kind.Integer. Schema annotation strings never confer authority/provenance. Enforce finite digit/scale/atom limits during admission, lexical parsing and arithmetic before large allocations where possible, and bound map-key hashing/comparison and serialization/output formatting. An already allocated caller BigInteger is not retroactively bounded. The six members and exact-decimal implementation are proposal-only; no production implementation is claimed, and finite defaults/accepted numeric limits remain unselected. These unresolved policy/implementation items support Revise."
    },
    {
      "id": "O2-Q2",
      "answer": "Preserve IsList independently of atom count: empty and singleton lists remain lists; neither becomes absent value or scalar. Preserve each atomic item's selected type/provenance so union-member selection is not lost. Keep nilled, HasNoTypedValue and an empty typed list distinct. Original PSVI/assessment remains original evidence; fresh construction may issue current constructed type evidence but no original assessment. The proposed shape represents these distinctions, but the audited native backend establishes only an exact-decimal profile and does not establish general list/union, union-of-lists or all XSD 1.1 typed-value coverage. Return explicit Unsupported for unimplemented backend/profile cases; that does not remove the required representation contract. No additional required type/member is identified from the reviewed packet, but implementation and profile qualification remain open."
    },
    {
      "id": "O2-Q3",
      "answer": "For N1/N8, component/source/snapshot/query identities must remain distinct; actual authority membership and same-component comparison are provider-verified, never inferred from names, GUIDs or digests. For N2, derivation, affiliation and complete component closure return Supported only for complete provider answers; otherwise Unsupported, never false/empty as a success-shaped fallback. For N3/N5, retain governing type, original node facts/PSVI, list/union shape and per-atomic provenance, with nil/no-typed-value distinctions. For N4, bind the advisor to an immutable effective environment (host/version, XDM revision, behavior profile and normalized static context) and a fixed assessment episode (date/time/timezone); unsupported assertion/CTA routes remain explicitly Unsupported. For N7, raw work and deferred consumption stay within the admitted operation lifetime, with actual provider resource ownership kept separate from engine admission/revocation. The proposal contains corresponding authority, advisor, context, episode and lifetime shapes; current Schema implementation does not qualify them generally. No extra required member is identified from the BCAP delta, but exact finite numeric defaults, adopted semantic/profile coverage and source-backed implementation remain unresolved, so this is not an acceptance."
    },
    {
      "id": "O2-Q4",
      "answer": "Compatibility is directional and must be established for exact source and target advisors under the exact execution environment. A compatible view preserves original source facts/PSVI and does not rewrite provenance. Return Incompatible only where a supported complete proof establishes it; return Unsupported where proof is incomplete. QName, digest or descriptive-label equality is never proof. The reviewed Schema backend has no qualified general cross-universe compatibility route; such routes are refused as Unsupported pending provider evidence. The proposed compatibility authority/view signatures express the design boundary, but are proposal-only and have no positive runtime proof. No additional signature gap is identified from the current packet; provider support, explicit profile decisions and R4 positive runtime evidence remain pending."
    }
  ],
  "unresolvedRequiredSignatureGaps": [],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "kind": "DesignDisposition",
      "reference": "BCAP manifest ff475d712f6ef6aa5033113cc39afb887ae4cbad24705098c5c9cb2097641688; REVIEW.md R01-R08; O2 questions in PACKETS.json; proposal inputs/proposal/ExactNumeric.cs.txt and Provider.cs.txt. Proposed declaration bodies are not production execution."
    },
    {
      "kind": "SourceMapping",
      "reference": "Bosak.Schema public source revision 20090180755d0427d824b091cf838e9a03ca9adc; public docs/XSD11_GAP_MATRIX.md and docs/AGENT_HANDOVER.md record incomplete XSD 1.1/backend and core session/PSVI integration."
    },
    {
      "kind": "DesignDisposition",
      "reference": "Bosak/docs/foundation-r2-ledger/DECISIONS.md D07-D10 and D12; Bosak/docs/foundation-r2-ledger/REQUIREMENTS.md N1-N8 remain pending owner acceptance."
    },
    {
      "kind": "DesignDisposition",
      "reference": "Bosak/docs/release-planning/OWNER-CAPABILITIES.md: bounded decimal-only native profile, no established general list/union or compatible-universe route, and explicit need to represent unsupported backend cases."
    }
  ],
  "runtimeQualification": false,
  "c45Accepted": false,
  "apiFrozen": false,
  "priorReturnId": "O2-Schema",
  "reviewMode": "MissingFullReturn",
  "deltaApplicability": "R01: capture is an XSLT output route and does not widen Schema numeric or compatible-view support. R02: principal/secondary serialized output, properties and messages are not typed XDM values or PSVI and must not be used to infer Schema provenance. R03: preserve original provider failures and keep them separate from typed-value/assessment outcomes; a captured output does not convert Unsupported or Invalid into success. R04: existing finite snapshot/atom/digit/scale controls are design intents, not selected workload defaults; parsing, arithmetic, map-key work and serialization need bounded policy, while no new Schema-specific capture limit is accepted here. R05: typed values and their provider evidence are borrowed within the exact admitted operation; capture does not transfer authority or extend resource lifetime. R06: raw exception graphs remain local diagnostics and are not traversed or serialized as schema evidence. R07: Core cost measurements are observations, not accepted Schema performance budgets; actual Schema numeric, list/union and compatibility workloads remain unqualified. R08: this is Revise for the exact design review; no public SDK/runtime support, C45, API freeze or product release acceptance is implied.",
  "originalExceptionGraphDisposition": "Exception, Data and InnerException graphs are local diagnostic references only, not immutable/detached schema evidence and not safe for IPC. Preserve object identity and aggregate boundaries for local diagnosis; do not recursively inspect provider objects, treat exception payloads as schema facts, or traverse nodes after admission revocation. Do not serialize or publish raw exception graphs. Any external diagnostic projection requires a separate owner-controlled bounded allowlist/redaction policy. Exception retention does not establish typed-value validity, authority, compatibility or successful cleanup.",
  "acceptedPerformanceBudgets": null,
  "priorResponseSha256": null
}
```
